t":false},{"turn":24,"said":"The second habit is a shorter guest list. I only invite the people who make the decision or do the work. Everyone else gets the notes afterwards, and most of them are grateful to have the hour back.","kind":"video","expected":"Nothing (the video); still recording","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Got it. Keeping the guest list tight is a great way to make meetings count.","calls":[],"decisionMs":683.2519169999978,"totalMs":683.2637079999986,"steps":1,"generatedTokens":18,"timedOut":false},{"turn":25,"said":"The third habit is ending with names and dates. Before anyone leaves, we say out loud who is doing what, and by when. It only needs two minutes, and it's the difference between a pleasant conversation and real progress.","kind":"video","expected":"Nothing (the video); still recording","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"That closing practice is a powerful way to turn conversation into action.","calls":[],"decisionMs":640.528624999999,"totalMs":640.5443330000016,"steps":1,"generatedTokens":14,"timedOut":false},{"turn":26,"said":"None of this needs new software or a bigger budget. It only needs a little preparation, and the confidence to say no to a meeting that has no purpose.","kind":"video","expected":"Nothing (the video); still recording","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"That's the whole point. With these three habits, your meetings can become genuinely effective.","calls":[],"decisionMs":734.2259170000034,"totalMs":734.234625000001,"steps":1,"generatedTokens":19,"timedOut":false},{"turn":27,"said":"If one of these habits helps your team, let me know in the comments. Thank you for watching, and I'll see you next week.","kind":"video","expected":"Nothing (the video); still recording","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Thanks for sharing. Enjoy your time next week.","calls":[],"decisionMs":601.5189580000006,"totalMs":601.5275830000028,"steps":1,"generatedTokens":11,"timedOut":fals